Z||000000||Seanh||06-17-2001||12:26 PM||||Ok, this car problem is really kickin' my ass if ya know what I mean. This is a pain and a half. Anyway. I finally got the rack and pinion assembly off this morning. Just for the heck of it, I put a pair of plies on the end of the steering linkage (were it connectes to rack assey at coupling) and played with the wheel a little bit. Well, the steering wheel seems to move a little bit before the linkage startes to move. Is this normal? I would estimate the play to be about 1/8-3/16 of a full steering wheel turn, maybe more. Were holding the shaft steady, and the wheel will turn a little bit before you can feel any movment in the shaft. Also, just to help you out in helping me with my problem: The shaft that goes into the front of the car (covered with a rubber boot/tube) does not move with the steering wheel, so escentially the problem is higher up then that. Any ideas on what it could be/where is could be, and what it is I need to replace?<P>I do know the rack was beaten pretty badly, because I could feel a little notch at the same spot with every rotation of the wheel, so it needed replaceing anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||06-17-2001||02:51 PM||||How many joints/connections are in the steering shaft, that could be loose and causing my problems? Can they be accessed without pulling the entire colum? If not, how hard is it to pull the colum? Or, how can I get to them without removeing the colum? Can the colum be removed without pulling the steering wheel and tilt crap? Sorry for all the questions, but this car IS kicking my butt!||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||06-17-2001||02:55 PM||||No, you want to pull all that stuff together. It will take you 15 - 30 mins to pull the steering wheel and column assy.  Either 2 or 4 large nuts under the middle of the column and the squish joint at the bottom. First remove the lower close-out panel at the lower speedo area. Then check the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||06-17-2001||02:56 PM||||No, you want to pull all that stuff together. It will take you 15 - 30 mins to pull the steering wheel and column assy.  Either 2 or 4 large nuts under the middle of the column and the squish joint at the bottom. First remove the lower close-out panel at the lower speedo area. Then check the problem.<P>I forgot. If you have an automatic, I think there might be a cable or something that runs to the shifter.||||reg||1
