Z||000011||Seanh||06-17-2001||07:52 PM||||Alright. I unbolted the colum from the car, and sat it in the seat for now. I still haven't removed the interlock, so I can't move the colum far.<P>Anyway, my discoveries: The problem in no visable! Sucks for me! Apperently the gears that are stripped are under the black caseing, so how do I get to them? Would it be easier to buy a new colum, and swap steering wheels? How much can I get one for? How expensive is it going to be to fix mine? I'm still just baffled about getting the case off the colum to acess the problem gears. I really don't want to remove the steering wheel, and tilt wheel crap! If I do indeed remove the steering wheel, should I scribe an alignment mark, or will it be useless since I'm tearing this all apart anyway? Thanks!<P>Email me quickly please if you have a colum for an 86 GT or compatable for sale cheap!||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||06-17-2001||11:11 PM||||It's been awhile.....<P>carefully inspect where the cable enters the tan/offwhite plastic shell of the interlock. You should see a latch tab on the black cable. Depress that tab and the cable should come out of the shell with minimal BS. Otherwise you'll have to follow the information in my cave article.<P>The play can be one of 5 places.<P>1,2 the two U joints in the lower shaft.<BR>3 the plastic ball in the tilt unit.<BR>4 a junked bearing<BR>5 the telescopics could be sloppy. Very rare.<P>The first 3 are most likely.<P>Well... one more, the wonderfull bolts that hold the tilt unit. They may be loose enough to allow some play w/o the obvious flopping yet.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Seanh||06-18-2001||01:41 AM||||I did get the cable off, and the column completly off finally. Anyway, like Iv said, the passenger wheel/rim hit a railroad tie at about 15-20mph and it took the impact of the whole car pretty much on the passenger wheel, tire is trashed needless to say (looked like a Firestone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) Iv established that the play is located behind the steering wheel, and before where the shaft exits the caseing. I was thinking it could be a trashed brearing first off. The U joints in the lower shaft are visible, like not in the case right? If so, they are not where the play is happening, its above there. As for the telescopics, if your talking about what I'm thinking of, then that is not the problem either, I don't think. Either way, do you think it would be easier to just swap another column into the car? ||||reg||1
