Z||000016||rogergarrison||06-18-2001||12:48 PM||||you could have just stripped off some splines at the top of the shaft that the steering wheel fits on. that would let the steering wheel move back and forth without moving the shaft. Aftermarket steering wheels especially have a problem staying tight since the shaft is slightly tapered. I have to tighten the lock nut at least once a year on mine.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Seanh||06-18-2001||01:53 PM||||Yep, I thought about that, so I checked it by removeing the hood button and holding the shaft while turning the wheel. The wheel is moving the shaft, but like I said, its inside the caseing, so pretty difficult to get to I would imagin. Thanks though. I do have an aftermarket wheel, and I too have tighten up the lock nut a couple times a year also.||||reg||1
